  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given three positive integers N,A,N, A,N,A, and BBB. Further, it is known that ∣A−B∣≤1|A-B| \\leq 1∣A−B∣≤1.\n\nCount the number of integers XXX such that:\n\n\n1≤X≤N1 \\leq X \\leq N1≤X≤N; and\nThere exist **non-negative integers** ppp and qqq satisfying the equation\nA⋅p+B⋅q=XA\\cdot p + B\\cdot q = XA⋅p+B⋅q=X\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case will contain three space-separated integers N,A,N, A,N,A, and BBB, as described in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of integers XXX satisfying the given condition.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤10181 \\leq N \\leq 10^{18}1≤N≤1018",
      "1≤A,B≤1091 \\leq A, B \\leq 10^91≤A,B≤109",
      "∣A−B∣≤1|A-B| \\leq 1∣A−B∣≤1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n7 3 4\n7 3 3\n7 3 2\n1109258281 19402 19401",
        "output": "4\n2\n6\n921068581",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: With A=3,B=4,A = 3, B = 4,A=3,B=4, and N=7N = 7N=7, we have the following valid XXX:\n\nX=3=1⋅3+0⋅4X = 3 = 1\\cdot 3 + 0\\cdot 4X=3=1⋅3+0⋅4\nX=4=0⋅3+1⋅4X = 4 = 0\\cdot 3 + 1\\cdot 4X=4=0⋅3+1⋅4\nX=6=2⋅3+0⋅4X = 6 = 2\\cdot 3 + 0\\cdot 4X=6=2⋅3+0⋅4\nX=7=1⋅3+1⋅4X = 7 = 1\\cdot 3 + 1\\cdot 4X=7=1⋅3+1⋅4\n\nTest case 222: For A=B=3A = B = 3A=B=3 and N=7N = 7N=7, only 3=1⋅3+0⋅33 = 1\\cdot 3 + 0\\cdot 33=1⋅3+0⋅3 and 6=1⋅3+1⋅36 = 1\\cdot 3 + 1\\cdot 36=1⋅3+1⋅3 are valid."
      }
    ]
